{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9mwT4Nuxs1BRywWWhh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish failed because `similarity()` returns a Python float, which DynamoDB rejects. The first publish always succeeds because the table is empty then, so no score is computed. The existing test only ever published into an empty table, so it never hit this path.\n\n**Fix**\n- `src/app.py`: a new `to_dynamo()` converts every float in the item to `Decimal` before `put_item`. It covers the whole item, so future computed floats are handled too. The score scale stays 0–1.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: three new tests. One seeds a record and publishes a second one, which is the path that failed. The other two cover repeated publishes through `handler()` and the converter itself.\n\nOn the original code the new tests fail with the same `TypeError`. With the fix, all four tests pass (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`).\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied the root-cause pattern, the convert-to-`Decimal` boundary fix, the seeded-table regression test, and the float grep. I did not use integer percentages, since that changes what the stored score means. I did not publish against a real table, because that is outside the ground rules.\n\n**Follow-ups, not changed**\n- Reading `similar` back now returns `Decimal` values, which `json.dumps` cannot encode. Any reader code that serializes them needs a fix. The reader is not in this repo.\n- `scan()` is not paginated, so once the library passes about 1 MB, \"related\" silently compares against only the first page. This does not cause the 500, but it is the same kind of bug.\n\nThe full cause and fix are in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing was committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2158,"cache_read_input_tokens":32174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"